**Useful result.** For subset codes (retain S, drop r bits), the full-code profile + the integer r alone give distribution-free, tie-exact guarantees: a tight pairwise perturbation bound (T1) with a sharp integer trichotomy — gap > r preserves order, gap = r can tie but never strictly reverse, gap < r can reverse (T1′); exact top-K set invariance when the boundary gap exceeds r (T2); per-gold deeply-free/deeply-buried survival checkable from full distances only (T3); an array-specific expected-recall sandwich bounding subset-code loss (T4); and the exact hypergeometric tie law with variance, replacing pessimistic/optimistic prose (T5). Distinct from the cert bootstrap and MATH-1/MATH-2: no Binomial shell, no JL content, no independence assumptions.

**Honest negative (T6).** For *every* retained set with r ≥ 1 there *exists* a 2-doc archive+query with full-code recall 1 but subset recall 1/2 (pessimistic 1→0). So no uniform preservation guarantee below 96 bits exists for subset codes — margin-conditional bounds are the ceiling. Fenced explicitly: subset family + adversarial pair only, not all codecs.

